      "sourceSemantics": "Reserves through durable inference.control, freezes exact App Server request/correlation, requires independently signed final-use authority and commits dispatch before the effect. New requests enter turn/start once. Completed duplicates return stored historical observations; uncertain reopen attempts use exact thread/read history without a new turn/start. Recovered observations retain prior usage, owner loss and cancelled/timed-out/quarantined local boundary; missing history or usage remains unknown. Intelligence-bound recovered terminals reconcile the exact existing Agentd target through observed-current-revision CAS; existing exact terminal receipts remain historical truth and conflicts deny local success. Historical missing authority frontiers quarantine before owner publication. Every denied nonterminal observation and cancellation intent is journaled before external cancellation or interruption awaits. Existing terminal owner receipts must match the same worker-boundary phase used for publication, without reading a live clock for matching historical facts. Prepared no-effect abort proofs are one-shot and bound to the exact issuing control instance, request and revision; foreign or reopened owners cannot consume them. Exact recovered physical terminal facts retain a bounded UTF-8 output prefix when provider text exceeds 1 MiB, quarantine logical success and permit terminal capacity settlement. Nonterminal recovery persists local cancellation before and after awaited reconciliation, including error exits; cancellation cannot become recovered success. Definitively unsent stops cannot later accept settlement observations or regain a slot. Optional cognitive queries and intelligence bindings are separate profiles: their combination is rejected before admission because current owner ports cannot revalidate both cuts together. The executable parses required flags, the complete intelligence group and supported profile combination before protected configuration, journal or stdin I/O; parser tests are not full executable E2E.",
